{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261111T185720Z-b9b125d3", "ts": "2026-11-11T19:01:57Z", "actor": {"worktree": "ci-pool", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "chore/ci-pool"}, "body": {"base_commit": "1cbc805d868b7f6838b952991f0f99d3a02bd516", "base_tree": "1145fb361249b5218943e346a7b0c1f647a5912b", "head_tree": "78c7a87014fbe75f6125d74cca14986352df928a", "head_commit": "00711c1e23ad2b98f5394a8e11b315f9bdf92799", "dispatch_commit": "00711c1e23ad2b98f5394a8e11b315f9bdf92799", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".github/workflows/ci.yml", ".github/workflows/release.yml", ".test_durations", "docs/testing.md", "scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh", "scripts/ci-unit-tests.sh", "scripts/update-test-durations.sh", "tests/enforcement/test_ci_doc_only_skip.py", "tests/enforcement/test_ci_unit_shards.py"], "files_changed": [".github/workflows/ci.yml", ".github/workflows/release.yml", ".test_durations", "docs/testing.md", "scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh", "scripts/ci-unit-tests.sh", "scripts/update-test-durations.sh", "tests/enforcement/test_ci_doc_only_skip.py", "tests/enforcement/test_ci_unit_shards.py"], "files_oracle": [], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "No test evidence for the reviewed tree: prawduct-hook test-status reports 'stale: no .test-evidence.json on disk', and nothing on record shows the pool route has completed a run end to end", "recommendation": "Scope: instance -- evidence was never recorded for this branch. Run the suite on this tree (the enforcement tests in tests/enforcement/test_ci_unit_shards.py and test_ci_doc_only_skip.py at least) and record evidence; link the first green `unit (testament pool)` and `unit (evals-N)` runs in the PR body so the route is shown working, not only pinned by string tests.", "files": ["tests/enforcement/test_ci_unit_shards.py", "tests/enforcement/test_ci_doc_only_skip.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "The required gate on the pool runs without --fresh or --no-cache, so warm-container state or cache-served results can satisfy `check`, and docs list only two differences from the shards", "recommendation": "Scope: instance -- scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh:73 calls `testament run --json=summary --junit-xml ... --no-fallback` only; the client's own help names --fresh 'for a merge or release gate' and says that without --no-cache a project the coordinator serves from cache gets earlier passing results marked served. Whether the merge gate executes every test therefore depends on a coordinator-side grant this repo cannot see. Decide: pass --fresh (and --no-cache if served results are unwanted on the gate), or state in docs/testing.md:103-107 that the pool route may serve cached passes and reuse warm containers, beside the two differences already listed.", "files": ["scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh", "docs/testing.md"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "warning", "title": "A pool outage turns every same-repo PR's required `check` red, and the only way back to the shards is deleting the TESTAMENT_KEY secret, which nothing documents", "recommendation": "Scope: instance -- route (.github/workflows/ci.yml:36) decides on the secret's presence alone, and --no-fallback (correctly) refuses to run locally, so an unreachable coordinator or console fails every run with no switch short of removing the secret and re-minting a key afterwards. Either let route read an Actions variable that forces the shards (e.g. route to the pool only when the key is present AND the variable does not say shards), or document the outage procedure in docs/testing.md's 'CI on the testament pool' section.", "files": [".github/workflows/ci.yml", "docs/testing.md"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "The refusal and retry paths of scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh, and the duration estimator in scripts/update-test-durations.sh, have no test", "recommendation": "Scope: class -- new CI shell scripts whose logic is exercised only on the happy path (every pool-route CI run). Untested: the non-200 refusal (ci-unit-pool.sh:44-50), the wheel-name and sha256 refusals (55-62), the retryable-envelope decision (74-88) and the summary's parsing of the envelope; and update-test-durations.sh's per-file estimate (52-) whose output only moves balance. test_ci_doc_only_skip.py already runs ci-scope.sh against fixtures; the same shape (a local http.server console plus stub `uv`/`testament` on PATH) would pin the digest refusal and the retry-once rule. Search scripts/*.sh for other CI scripts with branching logic and no test that executes them.", "files": ["scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh", "scripts/update-test-durations.sh"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "The wheel's sha256 is compared against a header from the same response, so it proves integrity, not that the build is the signed release's; docs and the script header read as an independent check", "recommendation": "Scope: instance -- ci-unit-pool.sh:53-62 reads X-Testament-Wheel-SHA256 from the same HTTPS response that carries the wheel; no signature is verified, so the trust root is TLS to the console (which also decides the verdict, so the practical risk is small). Make the claim relational at ci-unit-pool.sh:20-23 and docs/testing.md:94-96: the digest catches a truncated or corrupted download; authenticity rests on the console's TLS.", "files": ["scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh", "docs/testing.md"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "ci-unit-pool.sh sends the client key as a bearer header to whatever TESTAMENT_CONSOLE names without refusing a non-https URL", "recommendation": "Scope: instance -- console comes from an Actions variable (ci-unit-pool.sh:41-46); an http:// value set by mistake would send TESTAMENT_KEY in cleartext. A `case \"$console\" in https://*) ;; *) refuse` before the curl closes it.", "files": ["scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "Keeping the key off fork PRs rests on GitHub's default secret policy, not on anything the workflow asserts", "recommendation": "Scope: instance -- the trigger is pull_request (not pull_request_target), so a public repo's fork PRs get no secrets and route picks the shards, as ci.yml:26 and docs/testing.md say. If the repo were ever private with 'send secrets to fork pull requests' enabled, a fork's own ci-unit-pool.sh would run holding the key. route could also require github.event_name == 'push' or the PR head repo to equal github.repository before choosing the pool.", "files": [".github/workflows/ci.yml"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "scripts/ci-scope.sh's header still says only `check` and each `unit` shard run it, now that unit-pool does too", "recommendation": "Scope: instance -- scripts/ci-scope.sh:6-7 names the jobs that run it; the diff added a third (unit-pool) and updated test_ci_doc_only_skip.py's docstring but not this header. Make it relational ('every job that skips on a doc-only PR') rather than adding a name. Wording only; nothing reads it.", "files": ["scripts/ci-scope.sh"], "fid": "R-8"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 4, "note": 4}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `chore/ci-pool`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "1cbc805d868b7f6838b952991f0f99d3a02bd516", "record_lint": {"records": ["docs/testing.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap":